3. CORE WORKFLOWS

   A. DRIVER FLOW
      1. Sign up → Firebase Auth
      2. Add vehicle details (battery, connectors)
      3. Search nearby charging points
         - Query Firestore for chargingPoints within radius
         - Filter by connector type, availability, price
         - Use Google Maps API for distance & routing
      4. View point details & reviews
      5. Reserve charging point
         - Create reservation doc with status: "reserved"
         - Set expiresAt = now + 30 minutes
         - Generate QR code token
      6. Navigate to location (Google Maps)
      7. Arrive at location
         - Scan QR code or enter connector ID
         - Update reservation status: "confirmed"
      8. Start charging
         - For company stations: partner API triggers charging
         - For private hosts: driver plugs in, host verifies
         - Create chargingSession doc
      9. Charging completes
         - For private hosts: meter reading captured (photo or IoT)
         - Calculate kWh consumed
         - Create payment record
      10. Rate & review host/point

   B. HOST FLOW (Existing Station)
      1. Sign up → Firebase Auth
      2. Select "Existing charging station"
      3. Enter partner company & station ID
      4. Verify ownership (email from company account)
      5. Configure commission split with ImCharge
      6. Sync availability from partner API
      7. Monitor reservations in real-time
      8. Receive commission payouts weekly/monthly

   C. HOST FLOW (Private Host)
      1. Sign up → Firebase Auth
      2. Select "Private charging point"
      3. Enter location (address, geopoint)
      4. Upload photos of location
      5. Add charging equipment details
         - Brand, model, power (kW)
         - Connector types
         - Meter serial number
      6. KYC verification (identity + address)
      7. Set pricing (€/kWh)
      8. Set availability hours
      9. For each reservation:
         - Verify driver arrival (QR code scan)
         - Allow driver to plug in
         - Capture meter reading at start & end (photo or app)
         - Confirm session completion
      10. Receive payment after meter verification
      11. Payout to bank account

4. RESERVATION STATE MACHINE

   States:
   - available: Charging point ready to book
   - reserved: Driver holds slot for 30 min (expiresAt = now + 30 min)
   - confirmed: Driver arrived, QR scanned, reservation locked
   - charging: Charging session active
   - completed: Session finished, payment processed
   - cancelled: Reservation expired or user cancelled

   Transitions:
   available → reserved (on create_reservation)
   reserved → confirmed (on qr_scan or connector_id_verified)
   reserved → available (on expiry or cancel_reservation)
   confirmed → charging (on charging_started)
   charging → completed (on charging_ended + payment_confirmed)
   charging → disputed (on meter_reading_mismatch or payment_failure)
   [any] → cancelled (on user_cancellation)

5. PAYMENT FLOW

   A. Company Station (Commission Model)
      1. Driver reserves & charges
      2. Partner API confirms session & kWh
      3. Partner charges driver (outside ImCharge)
      4. Partner reports transaction to ImCharge
      5. ImCharge calculates commission (e.g., 15%)
      6. ImCharge invoices partner or receives commission
      7. Host receives payout from partner (not ImCharge)

   B. Private Host (Metered Billing Model)
      1. Driver reserves & confirms arrival
      2. Host verifies driver & meter reading (start)
      3. Driver charges
      4. Host captures meter reading (end)
      5. ImCharge calculates kWh: (end - start) / 1000
      6. ImCharge calculates amount: kWh × pricePerKwh
      7. ImCharge charges driver via Stripe
      8. ImCharge retains commission (e.g., 20%)
      9. ImCharge pays host: amount × (1 - 0.20)
      10. Payout processed weekly/monthly

